{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5f9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e76-bae7-71e0-a570-bb4cc0067a43"},"sequence":343,"recorded_at":1780531400000681,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"45fd7c01-9695-4667-a2dd-8bdcc25383b6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"45fd7c01-9695-4667-a2dd-8bdcc25383b6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"45fd7c01-9695-4667-a2dd-8bdcc25383b6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"cfc9994f-3d95-49ed-875c-06664cd4bc36"},"task_id":"cfc9994f-3d95-49ed-875c-06664cd4bc36","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"cfc9994f-3d95-49ed-875c-06664cd4bc36","chunk":"Read text file `internal/provider/doc.go`.\n1|// Package provider implements the M0 trusted provider plugin host boundary\n2|// of pinned specification Section 7.1: deterministic executable discovery,\n3|// trust recording, and substitution detection.\n4|//\n5|// The actor every Section 7.1 RFC 2119 keyword governs here is the ax host\n6|// (this repository). The provider plugin is a child process this package\n7|// never builds, probes, or executes: Discover takes no probe or execution\n8|// callback, so the Section 7.1 duplicate refusal structurally happens before\n9|// any probe or execution. Later leaves own the wire protocol (Section 7.2),\n10|// manifests and capabilities (Sections 7.3-7.7, 8), and process lifecycle.\n11|//\n12|// This package is an internal M0 host boundary, not a public stable plugin\n13|// SDK: Section 7.1 states that M0 MUST NOT advertise a public stable plugin\n14|// SDK, so no exported symbol offers plugin authorship, version negotiation,\n15|// or compatibility promises. The package lives under internal/ and declares\n16|// no stability contract.\n17|//\n18|// Discovery consumes only operator configuration (providers.plugin_dirs in\n19|// listed order, built-in adapters, then PATH when allow_path_plugins is\n20|// true) and the host filesystem. Everything crossing that boundary is\n21|// treated as attacker-influenced: a failed or partial read is reported as a\n22|// failure, never as an absence that a fallback could treat as satisfied.\n23|//\n24|// The package mutates no durable state of its own. Trust returns a\n25|// TrustRecord value the host persists; Verify rechecks that receipt against\n26|// freshly read filesystem facts. There is therefore no crash or idempotency\n27|// surface inside this package: repeated Discover calls over an unchanged\n28|// tree return identical candidates, and Verify is a pure recheck.\n29|//\n30|// A discovered candidate carries no availability, status, or capability\n31|// claim. Discovery answers which executable serves a provider ID; whether\n32|// any capability is available is decided by the probe plane (a later leaf),\n33|// never advertised here.\n34|package provider"}}}
